oh-sing-o-sing-this-blessed-morn-nativit.body:
Verse 1:
[C]Sing, O sing, this [F]blessed [C]morn,
[F]Unto us [Am]a [G7]Child is [C]born,
[Am]Unto us a [E]Son is [Am]giv'n,
[D7]God Himself [Em]comes [G]down from Heav'n.

Refrain:
[F]Sing, O [C]sing, this [F]blessed [C]morn,
Jesus Christ to[F]day is [C]born.

Verse 2:
[C]Jesus Christ, the [F]King of [C]kings,
[F]Maker of [Am]all [G7]worldly [C]things,
[Am]Now descends from [E]Heav'n to [Am]Earth,
[D7]To restore [Em]us [G]by His birth;

Verse 3:
[C]God of God, and [F]Light of [C]Light,
[F]Comes with mer[Am]cies [G7]infi[C]nite;
[Am]Joining in a [E]wondrous [Am]plan
[D7]Heav'n to earth [Em]and [G]God to Man;

Verse 4:
[C]God with us, Em[F]manu[C]el,
[F]Deigns for ev[Am]er [G7]now to [C]dwell;
[Am]He on Adam's [E]fallen [Am]race
[D7]Sheds the full[Em]ness [G]of His Grace;

Verse 5:
[C]Truth and Mercy [F]show their [C]face,
[F]And with lov[Am]ing [G7]kiss em[C]brace;
[Am]Righteousness looks [E]down from [Am]Heav'n,
[D7]God is pleased [Em]and [G]Man forgiv'n;

Verse 6:
God comes down that man may rise, Lifted far above the skies
He is Son of Man, that we Sons of God in Him may be;

Verse 7:
Human flesh is now become Christ's abode, the Godhead's home;
Royal Palace, sacred shrine For the Majesty Divine;

Verse 8:
Now we rise, from prison free; On we march to victory,
Joyful banners are unfurled; 'Tis the Birthday of the World;

Verse 9:
Now behold the rising Sun Hath His glorious race begun;
Now the Bridegroom from above Weds the Bride, with heavenly love;

Verse 10:
O renew us, Lord, we pray, With Thy Spirit day by day;
That we ever one may be With the Father, and with Thee;

Verse 11:
Sing, O sing this blessed Morn, Jesus Christ to-day is born;
Glory to the Father give, Praise the Son in whom we live;
Glory to the Spirit be, Godhead One, and Persons Three.
